<BaseLayout title="Driving">
  <h1>Driving</h1>
  <p>This section covers normal vehicle operation, drive settings, transmission behavior, driver assistance, braking, and handling. Equipment and available settings vary with drivetrain and options.</p>

  <h2>Before driving</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Adjust the seat, steering wheel, mirrors, and climate settings before moving.</li>
    <li>Check that doors and the tailgate are closed and that all occupants are properly restrained.</li>
    <li>Review any warning messages shown at startup; do not ignore a warning that indicates a safety-critical fault.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Engine and transmission</h2>
  <p>The T5 designation identifies the turbocharged gasoline powertrain in this model year. Drive smoothly until the engine and drivetrain reach normal operating temperature. If the transmission behaves unexpectedly, note the selected drive mode, engine temperature, speed, and warning messages before seeking diagnosis.</p>

  <h2>Drive modes and start/stop</h2>
  <p>Available drive settings and start/stop behavior depend on the vehicle's configuration and software. Consult the owner's manual for the controls fitted to the car. Do not assume a menu or button shown in another S60 is present on this vehicle.</p>

  <h2>Driver assistance</h2>
  <p>Driver-support features are assistance systems, not autonomous driving. Their presence and operation depend on installed options, road markings, weather, sensor condition, and system limitations. The driver remains responsible for controlling the vehicle and monitoring traffic.</p>

  <h2>Warning messages</h2>
  <p>Record the exact wording and any accompanying symbol. If a warning calls for stopping, reduced speed, or immediate service, follow the instruction in the vehicle and the owner's manual. Do not continue driving when braking, steering, tire, or powertrain behavior makes the car unsafe.</p>

  <h2>Reference source</h2>
  <p>See the <a href="https://www.volvocars.com/us/support/car/s60/18w46">official Volvo S60 owner's information</a> for the full operating instructions and system limitations.</p>
</BaseLayout>
